{
  "_note": "How each section is played (docs/power-chord-engine-brief.md §6). `register`: low = the key's lowest comfortable zone (open strings when the key has them), lift = chorusLift frets higher (engine-settings.json). `shapes`: voicing-shapes.json ids the path search may use. `rhythms`: per feel, a list of variants; seed 0 plays the first, regenerate cycles through them. Rhythm cells, 8 per bar (eighth notes): D = downstroke, U = upstroke, x = dead strum, - = let the last hit ring, . = rest. `articulation` per bar (cycled): pm = palm-muted, ring = let ring. `accents`: accented cells in every bar. `pushes`: bars whose last cell plays the next bar's chord an eighth early. `stopBar`: a full-band stop after that bar's first hit (N.C.). Song Engine v2 Phase 4 (DECISIONS.md): a bar is 8 cells, or 16 (sixteenths) where a groove needs them (gallops, fills); accents stay in eighths (0–7). `all` is a rhythm for every feel without its own. `drums` (per bar, cycled; null = the feel's template) is the groove's own kit in the bar's grid, so kicks land with the accents (R13). `stopCells` (per bar, cycled; null = none) is a full-band stop after that cell. Intro `riff` variants write a line from scale steps over each bar's chord (lib/riffs.ts); `requires: \"openRoots\"` limits one to songs whose Intro chords sit on open strings.",
